  - unicode-ident is (MIT OR Apache-2.0) AND Unicode-3.0. Unicode 3.0 is a
    permissive license that requires its copyright/permission notice to
    accompany copies; that notice is shipped as LICENSE-UNICODE in the crate.
  - linux-raw-sys and rustix offer Apache-2.0 (with LLVM exception) or plain
    Apache-2.0 or MIT; memchr offers Unlicense or MIT; r-efi offers MIT,
    Apache-2.0 or LGPL-2.1-or-later. Each has Apache-2.0/MIT-compatible terms.
  - option-ext 0.2.0 is MPL-2.0 (file-level copyleft). It is a direct,
    all-target dependency of dirs-sys 0.5.0 and is used unmodified; the full
    MPL-2.0 text ships in the crate as LICENSE.txt. Keep that notice with any
    distribution that includes it and keep any modifications to MPL files
    under MPL-2.0.
  - thiserror and thiserror-impl appear twice: 1.0.69 is used directly by
    buddy-core, and 2.0.21 is a transitive dependency of redox_users (a
    Redox-target-only dependency of dirs-sys). Both are MIT OR Apache-2.0.
  - The three workspace crates (buddy-core, buddy-cli, buddy-desktop) are
    first-party Apache-2.0 and are not listed here.
   - The fifteen crates added for the CLI harness (anstream, anstyle,
