the docs.rs 0.27.0 page (MIT, x86_64-pc-windows-msvc), the published crate
source downloaded from crates.io (Cargo.toml.orig `license = "MIT"`,
LICENSE.txt, README.md, examples/record.rs and the device-backed error tests),
the upstream repository README/examples/commits, and the Microsoft "Loopback
Recording" and "Exclusive-Mode Streams" documents.

The published README lists "Loopback capture" and shared/exclusive modes.
Upstream 0.27.0 sets `AUDCLNT_STREAMFLAGS_LOOPBACK` when an `AudioClient` from a
render endpoint is initialised with `Direction::Capture` in shared mode, and
returns `WasapiError::LoopbackWithExclusiveMode` for the exclusive-mode
combination. Microsoft's loopback document confirms that loopback works without
a virtual cable (it uses a hardware loopback pin when present, otherwise copies
the audio-engine output), that it is shared-mode only, and that event-driven
loopback clients are supported on Windows 10 version 1703 and later. Buddy's
System track therefore opens the default render endpoint in shared loopback
mode; the Mic track opens the default capture endpoint. No virtual loopback
device is installed or required. Exclusive-mode limitation: an application that
holds an endpoint exclusively seizes it and silences other applications; a
shared-mode loopback stream cannot capture that application's audio.

